Z||000002||hugh||11-28-2000||11:02 PM||||I'm not looking to pick it apart,but if it draws 50 amps as they say the alternator will immediately increase output because the voltage regulator will sense the voltage drop caused by the electrical load.It takes horsepower to spin that alternator and maintain the proper voltage.If the voltage drops the motor slows down,Also the relay they show in their drawing is a typical Bosch 30 amp relay which can cause a voltage drop.||||reg||1
