Z||000004||ebhan||06-10-2001||02:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>I'm not looking to pick it apart,but if it draws 50 amps as they say the alternator will immediately increase output because the voltage regulator will sense the voltage drop caused by the electrical load.It takes horsepower to spin that alternator and maintain the proper voltage.If the voltage drops the motor slows down,Also the relay they show in their drawing is a typical Bosch 30 amp relay which can cause a voltage drop.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>One could consider disabling the alternator charge/sense capability while in "boost" mode (mostly during acceleration). This is something you can’t do with regular (mechanical driven) super chargers.<P>One could even consider installing a dedicated battery just for "boot" mode that can be recharged while "in cruse" mode. This may allow one to use several hundred Amps while accelerating? Significant power increase could be reached (25-50%) ??<P>Has anyone done some experiments?<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Kwez||06-10-2001||02:24 PM||||mmm, I don't know if this is the same one, but the name is the same ...<BR>I have heard of this before, and it seemed to be basically crap (others' opinion) !!<P>I don't have any 1st hand experience w. it, but I would strongly urge anybody considering getting one to find out about it from someone who has had experience w. it.<P>You might try the Subaru Msg Board, I think some guys there might have looked it up before : <A HREF="http://www.i-club.com/cgi-bin/ubb6/ultimatebb.cgi" TARGET=_blank>http://www.i-club.com/cgi-bin/ubb6/ultimatebb.cgi</A> <P>Good luck||||reg||1
